cludes(column));\n  if (missingRequired || fields.length !== header.length) {\n    throw new IngestError(\"errors.rowShape\", { row: index + 1 });\n  }\n}\n```\n\nI classify this as a **bug**, as the input in form of a correctly formatted file (with allowed empty lines) should not fail the import process.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"issue\": 4406,\n  \"label\": \"bug\",\n  \"file\": \"src/ingest/parser.ts\",\n  \"evidence\": \"The assertShape function throws an error when an input line (due to an ending newline) has a different number of fields than the header in src/ingest/parser.ts.\"\n}\n```\n\nI will now return this finding.", "agent": "investigator-4406", "parent": "coordinator"}
